# Trivy ignore file for springboot-eks-api.
#
# Format:
#   AVD-ID  # reason — expiry date if known
#
# Add accepted findings here ONLY after reviewing them.
# Each entry must carry a comment explaining the rationale.

# ── EKS public API endpoint ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The blueprint Tier 1 design uses a public EKS API endpoint with no NAT
# gateway or VPN. This is intentional: CI runners need to reach the API server
# to deploy workloads, and Tier 1 has no private networking.
# Mitigation: the API server access is controlled by aws-auth / IAM; the
# endpoint is not wide-open to arbitrary workloads.
# Action: move to endpoint_public_access=false + private endpoint when adding
# a NAT Gateway or AWS PrivateLink (Tier 2 enhancement).
AVD-AWS-0040  # EKS public endpoint — Tier 1 design, no NAT gateway
AVD-AWS-0041  # EKS public CIDR 0.0.0.0/0 — same rationale as AVD-AWS-0040

# ── EKS logging ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Trivy requires all five log types; we enable audit/api/authenticator which
# covers the security-relevant events. scheduler and controllerManager logs are
# high-volume and add cost without improving the security posture for this
# workload size.
# Action: enable all five when moving to full audit compliance (Tier 2).
AVD-AWS-0176  # EKS not all log types enabled — audit/api/authenticator are set
AVD-AWS-0178  # EKS cluster logging — same rationale as AVD-AWS-0176
